  "presentation_summary": [
    "21-year-old man was found unresponsive and severely bradycardic, with prehospital heart rate in the 40s and emergency-department ECG showing complete heart block.",
    "He had visited a Lyme-endemic area 2 weeks before presentation.",
    "Heart rate later dropped into the 20s and did not respond adequately to atropine, requiring isoproterenol, transcutaneous pacing, and transvenous pacing.",
    "Laboratory findings included CRP 17.7 mg/dL, NT-proBNP 1623 pg/mL, normal troponin, WBC 8.9 x10^9/L, sodium 147 mmol/L, and creatinine 1.07 mg/dL.",
    "Lyme serology showed total antibody EIA positive, IgM positive, and IgG negative. He improved with IV ceftriaxone and pacing support, with 1:1 conduction by day 7 and normal sinus rhythm on Holter at day 9."
  ],
